{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/308430-making-a-mummy","id":308430,"title":"Making a Mummy","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mummy: The Curse"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-11-10T12:15:11-08:00","id":308430,"title":"Making a Mummy","content":"I've seen this sort of thread before on rpg.net and I thought it'd be fun to make one regarding Mummies who, at the moment, are one of the more intimidating splats to conceive this sort of thing around for me. If you're willing to share your process, walk us through the creation of your mummy, the inspirations behind them, why you chose the things you did. It'd be great to provide an example of your processes and to see the kinds of Mummies you guys are making. I plan to attempt to make a Mummy shortly, and I'll be sure to post my results as well.<br /> <br /> Share away!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-10T12:38:11-08:00","id":308451,"title":"","content":"Nakhte is my Su-Menent, and he was inspired by two things; how cool the Scythians were (horse nomads from Iran who fought alongside both Alexander and the Romans - a little late for Mummies timeline, but a neat example of &quot;barbarians&quot;) and the desire to excuse a Cult originating with Nazi activity in North Africa. The rest of the character followed from these two elements.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-10T12:40:04-08:00","id":308453,"title":"","content":"I've already posted a few characters over at my 1001 story hooks thread: <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> .) Rekhetre was once one of the most popular of the Su-Menent, renowned for being a death priest of unusually high compassion. The Rite of Return, the most powerful feat of magic ever performed by men, wasn't strong enough to change her caring nature, and it was to noone's surprise when she declared her decree to be that of the Heart.<br /> <br /> Her experiences in Buddhist India gave her compassion focus and guidance, as she refined her beliefs and learned about the suffering inherent in all life. <br /> <br /> Millenia later, Rekhetre, still a priest of death, brings everlasting peace to those who need it - and, in the end, everyone does. She still means well, as she always did, which is why her methods of passing the sacrament of death on to others are gentle, but neither she nor her cult of extremists are particularly discriminating as to who they murder in the name of compassion. Sooner or later, they'll figure out some way of using modern weaponry for the purposes of sharing their sacrament with hundreds or even thousands of people all at once; and on that day, Rekhetre, a Bodhisattva who chose to live and feel and suffer for all eternity, so that others don't have to, will weep with joy for bringing peace to so many people.<br /> <br /> <br /> .) One of the PC's Arisen compatriots Arises with startlingly little of her original personality and identity left (Memory 0). She's little more than a vessel of her Judge, a puppet of the Divine Will of Duat. <br /> <br /> And yet - her actions, under the constant, strict guidance of the Lords of Duat, leave the world a better place. The mummy punishes sin as much as she rewards virtue. Those who violate the laws put forth by the Judges are corrected, and the world is a little bit of a safer place near her. <br /> <br /> Perhaps it would be best if all Arisen surrender their will and individuality to the Judges, as she did? Some of the Su-Menent certainly begin to see it that way. <br /> <br /> <br /> .) A particularly charismatic Falcon-Headed Tef-Aabhi gets it into his head that this degenerate age needs the true guidance of a firm-handed leader, someone imbued with the wisdom of ages. Someone like him. <br /> <br /> The Judges punish his attempts at reaching out with his cult, grasping the local infrastructure and subverting the culture like crazy, but his message rings true to like-minded Arisen, many of them followers of the Ba like him, as they start creating the first empire ruled by the Arisen. Many opposing Arisen cults are simply swallowed by the collective might of their secret societies. <br /> <br /> <br /> .) One of the PCs has, in the past, clashed with a charismatic Mesen-Nebu, whose political convictions are particularly at odds with those of most ex-citizens of the Stone Age. He seems to think that power should go to the people and that people should fight for their basic rights and similar ridiculous nonsense. He has been active around the Peasant's Revolt in England in 1381, the Labour revolts of France in 1831 and many others before.<br /> <br /> After the Occupy Movement, his methods have grown increasingly radical. Now his cult has found some way to reach the mainstream audience with their anti-capitalism message, and their numbers are stronger than ever. Something needs to be done.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> .) No Arisen has spoken to Hsekiu, Arisen of the Tef-Aabhi, in centuries. He lies, like so many of the Deathless, dead but dreaming. No cultists revere his image (and if they do, then in secret). No Arisen utter his name, even as a whisper. <br /> <br /> The guilds do not precisely remember why they are so afraid of calling him back to life. There are faint memories of blood .. pain ... fates worse than death, especially for the Deathless. His tomb remains undisturbed, and if the guilds have their way, it shall remain so forever. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> .) One of the PCs, preferably one with a high Intelligence trait, has, in his first life, been a guild member of a certain notoriety. His obvious brilliance manifested in a way that made him a creator of artifacts and objects of madness - as a Mesen-Nebu, he might have devised alchemical concoctions that altered the basic nature of humans. A brilliant Tef-Aabhi might have constructed buildings whose geometric attributes influenced the destinies of all nearby people. A Su-Menent might have been an expert creator of necromantic weapons of mass destruction. A scribe of the Sesha-Hebsu could have put down words and pictographs that were obvious blasphemies, devouring the minds of those who read them. Etc.<br /> <br /> The Shan'iatu thought long and hard before making the decision of granting him immortality, in the end, deciding that the PC's brilliance in his first life needed to be preserved.<br /> <br /> As an Arisen, unable to recall much of his past, and irrevocably changed by 6000 years of undeath, the PC might well be terrified by his accomplishments as a creator of monstrosities and terrors - or, alternately, willing to embrace his dark past fully.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-11T23:30:16-08:00","id":309904,"title":"","content":"Grandmother remembers nothing of her time in Irem save that the day she was chosen to join the Maa-Kep was the most important day of her life. She remembers nothing of being \u015eahin-Nekhenet, of guarding the troves of the Turkish Cult of the Falcon as the &quot;Instrument of the \u015eahinleri&quot; <br /> <br /> She only knows that it is the Shaheens are her kin, and that she is to protect them and their family crypt in the swamps of Louisiana. <br /> <br /> That she is a curse laid upon all who would dare raise a hand to they who share the blood of the Nameless Falcon.<br /> <br /> If only she knew what that meant.<br /> <br /> So, yeah, I'll never get to play her, but the idea is that she's a redneck mummy. I'm thinking that eventually my players will bump into her during another game set in New Calais.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Call Me <b>Ray</b>.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://southern-gothic.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Southern Gothic </a>- Welcome to New Calais","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/256-gnomish-american","name":"Gnomish American","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar256_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-13T14:31:53-08:00","id":311653,"title":"","content":"My group focused on historical figures and places, then attributed them to Irem. Working backwards like this gives the world a real feel for the &quot;secret history&quot; that your character was part of.<br /> <br /> I noted how Grigori Rasputin was nearly impossible to kill, maintained a small cult that grew in influence, and was noted to have many mystic powers. I determined that to his followers he was, in fact, Vosch: a zealot whose fanatical devotion to Iremi religion that his presence alone could crush lesser men.<br /> <br /> One of the others in my group determined that the entirety of Venice, Italy was a geomantic tomb for his mummy Marco, who takes the form of a golden, lion-headed angel in battle (the winged lion being the city symbol.). His cult is the city council, and when he arises he immediately assumes the role of the Doge of Venice. He was very angry when his Bucentaur, or state vessel, was destroyed by Napoleon's forces in 1798 (it served as the housing of his sahu while he slept).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Cxuog44JenzbN7GaAyRqDO4DXce9VGv6ybaCv9yYsPk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Simulacre: An Alternative Morality Stat for Prometheans</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/9523-the-alchemy-lab-homebrew-athanors\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew Athanors</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/887-metamurpho","name":"Metamurpho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar887_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}